{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">OPSYS function</span>\n","class":"manual","created":1470,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/310201","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/OPSYS-function.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/OPSYS-function.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"OPSYS-function\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">OPSYS function</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"OPSYS-function__section_N10024_N10021_N10001\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Identifies the operating system being used,\nso that a single version of a procedure can work differently under\ndifferent operating systems. Returns the value of that operating\nsystem. Valid values are &quot;UNIX&quot; and &quot;WIN32&quot;.</p>\n      <div class=\"note note note_note\" id=\"OPSYS-function__note_N1002E_N10024_N10021_N10001\"><span class=\"note__title\">Note:</span> For\nboth 32-bit and 64-bit Windows operating systems, OPSYS returns\nthe value &quot;WIN32&quot;.</div>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"OPSYS-function__syntax_GC19XQ2698423\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d154245e99\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"OPSYS-function__idGDN2OC2673577\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>OPSYS</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"OPSYS-function__example_GC19XR2698427\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d154245e125\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">This\nprocedure produces a listing of the files in your current directory.\nThe OPSYS function determines which operating system you are running,\nand uses the appropriate operating system command to produce the\ndirectory listing. The example shows the possible return values.</p>\n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <strong class=\"ph b\">r-opsys.p</strong>\n      </p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"OPSYS-function__idGDN2OE2673581\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>IF <strong class=\"ph b\">OPSYS = &quot;UNIX&quot;</strong> THEN UNIX ls.\nELSE IF <strong class=\"ph b\">OPSYS = &quot;WIN32&quot;</strong> THEN DOS dir.\nELSE MESSAGE <strong class=\"ph b\">OPSYS</strong> &quot;is an unsupported operating system&quot;.</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"OPSYS-function__notes_GC19XS2698435\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d154245e169\">Note</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">ABL supports\nan override option that enables applications that need to return\nthe value of MS-DOS for all Microsoft operating systems to do so.\nFor example, if you do not want the value WIN32 returned when the\nWindows operating system is recognized, you can override this return\nvalue by defining the Opsys key in the Startup section of the current\nenvironment, which may be in the registry or in an initialization\nfile. If the Opsys key is located, the OPSYS function returns the\nvalue associated with the Opsys key on all platforms. </p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"OPSYS-function__see-also_GC19XT2698439\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d154245e178\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"DOS-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/DOS-statement.html\">DOS statement</a>, <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"UNIX-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/UNIX-statement.html\">UNIX statement</a>, <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"PROCESS-ARCHITECTURE-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/PROCESS-ARCHITECTURE-function.html\">PROCESS-ARCHITECTURE function</a>, <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Preprocessor-name-reference.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Preprocessor-name-reference.html\">{ } Preprocessor name reference</a></p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"OPEN-QUERY-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/OPEN-QUERY-statement.html\">OPEN QUERY statement</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"OR-operator-bitwise.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/OR-operator-bitwise.html\">OR operator (bitwise)</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/310201","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":1318,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"OPSYS function","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/OPSYS-function.html","type":"Manual"}